---
import DocsNav from "../../components/DocsNav.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { docs, repositoryUrl } from "../../data/site";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Architecture | OrbitKV"
  description="OrbitKV ABI8 identities, token and fixed-state transactions, reclamation, and engine boundaries."
  active="Architecture"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p>
    <h1>One authority for snapshots, sharing, and reuse.</h1>
    <p>
      ABI8 compiles retention semantics into immutable token snapshots and
      separate generation-checked fixed-state transactions.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="docs-layout">
    <DocsNav active="Architecture" />
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Pipeline</h2>
      <pre><code>{`Attention / state retention semantics
    -> Retention IR
    -> Lifetime / head stripes
    -> LayoutProgram
    -> PhysicalPlan
    -> immutable SnapshotLease head
    -> tail / COW copy / write intents
    -> completion-gated publication
    -> detach + final-ref certificate
    -> backend ACK + reuse`}</code></pre>

      <h2>Generated layouts</h2>
      <table class="evidence-table-native">
        <thead><tr><th>Semantics</th><th>Layout</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Full</td><td><code>AppendOnly</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sliding</td><td><code>Periodic</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sink + Sliding</td><td><code>Pinned + Periodic</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Same Chunk</td><td><code>ResettableArena</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Per-head windows</td><td>Lifetime-normalized stripes</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Safety</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Logical identity is separate from physical slot and generation.</li>
        <li>Address programs are the only logical addressing authority.</li>
        <li>Reuse requires semantic death, reader completion, and backend commit.</li>
        <li>Unsupported semantics and engine contracts fail closed.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>ABI8 manager lifecycle</h2>
      <p>
        A request points at an immutable, generation-checked snapshot head.
        <code>prepare_batch</code> keeps a candidate private and returns tail,
        exact COW copy, and fresh-write intents. <code>submit_batch</code>
        validates exact backend receipts. <code>complete_batch</code> publishes
        every request head atomically only after completion evidence validates.
      </p>
      <p>
        Request and Prefix refs, reader pins, and the writer live on the page.
        Detach returns explicit mirror CLEAR/REPLACE actions; a reclamation
        certificate appears only when the final ref is gone. Ambiguous copy,
        launch, or completion outcomes enter fail-stop quarantine.
      </p>

      <h2>Current integration boundary</h2>
      <p>
        The modular Rust token/fixed-state core and exact 40-symbol C ABI8 wire
        retain host L2 GO. In addition, exact source <code>6f62a23</code> has a
        sealed H20 correctness record for the <code>OrbitKVPrefixCache</code>
        path: Qwen Full and GPT-OSS Full+SWA at B1/B4, 12 matched pairs over
        three epochs, using official SGLang v0.5.17 with page16 BF16 NHD eager
        FA3. It verifies exact outputs and request traces, seeded Prefix hits,
        final all-free drain, and advancing SWA retirement, reclamation, and
        wrap counters for every Hybrid pair. It does not cover relocation, MLA,
        fixed-state, overlap, Graph, speculation, distributed execution, or
        performance qualification.
      </p>
      <p>
        The production request-owned fixed-state seam remains host-qualified
        only for initial clear, forward-event propagation, and retire/clear/ACK.
        Replacement copy is covered only by coordinator and real-CPU-tensor
        host tests; its production trigger remains pending. GDN, KDA, ShortConv,
        and linear-attention bindings remain pending. Manager and state-pool
        handles are separate and provide no cross-handle atomicity.
      </p>

      <h2>Capability levels</h2>
      <p>
        OrbitKV reports compiler, host/ABI, GPU-primitive, engine-E2E,
        and production qualification separately. The{" "}
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/capability-matrix.md`}>
          Capability Matrix
        </a>{" "}
        is the normative boundary.
      </p>

      <h2>Records</h2>
      <div class="doc-grid">
        {docs.map((item) => (
          <div class="doc-card">
            <span>{item.key}</span>
            <h3>{item.name}</h3>
            <p>{item.detail}</p>
            <a href={item.href}>Open record →</a>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="doc-note">
        <strong>Boundary.</strong>
        <p>
          The sealed ABI8 Prefix record reports mean manager overheads of +7.37%
          and +11.87% for Full B1/B4, and +3.99% and +4.45% for Hybrid B1/B4.
          These are descriptive measurements: <code>performance_go=false</code>,
          with no speedup, memory-saving, or general replacement claim. The
          frozen 9233c06d ABI5-v5 snapshot remains historical scoped L4 evidence
          only. The separate ABI8 fixed-state scope boundary is unchanged. Relocation, MLA,
          fixed-state, overlap/Graph, speculation, multi-GPU, and disaggregation
          remain outside the sealed ABI8 record.
        </p>
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/capability-matrix.md`}>
          Current capability matrix
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
